==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|auction|-eer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|ɪə(ɹ)|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[individual]] who [[conduct]]s an [[auction]] [[on behalf of]] a [[vendor]], [[accept]]ing [[bid]]s to [[find]] the [[best]] [[price]] for the [[vendor]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=w:Zadie Smith|title=w:The Autograph Man |publisher=Penguin Books (2003)|page=102|passage=The '''auctioneer''', with his fruity, theatrical voice and his gavel, hits a block of wood in precisely the same spot, no matter the day.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jeanne Sahadi|title='Do I hear 6 figures? Sold!' Auctioneering can be a lucrative job ... if you know what you're selling.|magazine=w:CNN Money|url=https://money.cnn.com/2005/06/02/pf/sixfigs_auctioneer/index.htm|date=2005-06-02|passage=But there are many items that '''auctioneers''' sell every day in various garb: industrial equipment, autos and real estate, to name a few.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Lauren M. Johnson and Christina Zdanowicz|title=A gravestone missing for almost 150 years was being used as a marble slab to make fudge|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2021/09/24/us/gravestone-returned-after-missing-150-years-trnd/index.html|date=2021-09-24|passage=The '''auctioneer''' donated the monument to FOLHC and they got to work restoring his plot.}}

